-- #2110 / review finding S0-1: the ACCEPT half of `effect_arg_slot_launder.mdk`,
-- and this sprint's "feature + UNRELATED code still behaves" fixture
-- ([T-GLOBAL-TABLE]).  Everything below must check clean.
--
-- Two OVER-CORRECTION controls, both one edit away from the reject next door:
--
--   1. `unbare : Bare e -> (Unit -> <e> Unit)`.  Character-for-character the
--      signature shape that rejects for `Slot`; the only difference is that
--      `Bare`'s field row is `<e>` and `Slot`'s is `<Stdout | e>`.  `Bare`
--      guarantees no atoms, so the field is charged exactly what it performs
--      and the declaration is honest.  This is what pins the guarantee to the
--      DECLARATION rather than to "an argument of wrapper shape": a fix that
--      charged every row-kinded argument, or that read the atoms off the use
--      site, reddens here and nowhere else.
--   2. `widen : Slot e -> Slot e` and `rewrap : Slot e -> Slot e`.  The atoms
--      `Slot e` carries at the argument are carried right back out at the
--      return occurrence, so nothing escapes and the coverage rule is
--      satisfied.  A fix that counted argument-side atoms without checking
--      whether a return occurrence covers them reddens these two.
--   3. `inspect : Slot e -> Int` — an INSPECTOR that never runs the field.  It
--      has no non-argument occurrence of `e` at all, which is the
--      argument-only shape; that arm is interface-method-only by design (see
--      `checkArgEffVars`), so an ordinary top-level inspector must stay clean.
--      This is the shape the coverage rule would break most widely if the
--      argument-only arm ever escaped to top-level signatures: 34 declarations
--      in the compiler's own sources have it.
--
-- The tail half — `Pair`, `firstOf`, `sndOf`, `idString`, `constUnit` — declares
-- no row-kinded parameter, mentions no effect row, and never touches
-- `Slot`/`Bare`, yet its inferred schemes are in this fixture's golden.  A
-- change that perturbs ordinary elaboration while teaching the coverage walkers
-- about the per-parameter atom table shows up here even though none of that
-- code goes near a wrapper.
data Slot e = Slot (Unit -> <Stdout | e> Unit)

data Bare e = Bare (Unit -> <e> Unit)

-- (1) the same signature shape that rejects for `Slot`, over a wrapper that
-- guarantees nothing
unbare : Bare e -> (Unit -> <e> Unit)
unbare b = match b
  Bare f => f

-- (2) the atoms go straight back out at the return occurrence
widen : Slot e -> Slot e
widen s = s

rewrap : Slot e -> Slot e
rewrap s = match s
  Slot f => Slot f

-- (3) an inspector that never runs the field: no non-argument occurrence of `e`
inspect : Slot e -> Int
inspect s = 7

-- ── unrelated: no row-kinded parameter, no effect row, no wrapper ────────────
data Pair a b = MkPair a b

firstOf : Pair a b -> a
firstOf (MkPair a _) = a

sndOf : Pair a b -> b
sndOf (MkPair _ b) = b

idString : String -> String
idString s = s

constUnit : a -> Unit
constUnit x = ()
